+modulo 4; m has order (p-1)/2; the quadratic residues and their negatives
+partition F_p^*; hence the affine group acts regularly on unordered pairs.
+It checks the triangular-graph parameters and expands all four coordinates in
+every reported layer before comparing moments.  Thus it does not appeal to an
+external theorem or to the planted answer.
+
+Hardness and attacks.  A reference solver scans all admissible scales, uses
+each first moment to propagate its only possible shear, and checks the second
+moments.  The compact route instead forms 4*sum(x^2)-sum(x)^2, cancels shear,
+takes the canonical square root, and groups equal candidates across rows.
+Decoy rows are made from independently sampled automorphic PDSs, exactly the
+same distribution as the two planted rows.  The panel tests raw-moment
+outliers, a zero-shear greedy guess, uniform restarts, and a scale-one
+first-moment ansatz.  The successful polynomial-time reference scan is
+reported separately, as Track B requires.
