612:\section{Genuinely Nonabelian PDSs}
628:In order to show that a set of PDS parameters is genuinely nonabelian, we need to develop techniques for showing that no abelian PDS can exist with those parameters. The first technique requires that we define a character of an abelian group $G$: the map $\chi$ from $G$ to the multiplicative group $\C$ is called a character if $\chi$ is a homomorphism. The set of all characters of $G$ is denoted $G^*$. %Our objective in what follows is to provide techniques for demonstrating that no abelian PDSs can exist in certain circumstances: hence, if we can construct a nonabelian PDS $D$ in that circumstance, then $D$ is genuinely nonabelian.
