1044:\section{Nonabelian Techniques and Future Directions}
1047:The world of PDSs in nonabelian groups is relatively unexplored territory, especially when compared to the abelian case.  The main issue at the moment is that powerful techniques in the abelian setting -- such as Ma's Multiplier Theorem (Lemma \ref{multiplierthm}) -- simply do not hold when the group is nonabelian.  With respect to the Multiplier Theorem, there is a partial generalization to the nonabelian case due to Ma \cite{Ma_1984}:  
