Step 0 survives only as Track B. The paper contains no distributional hardness theorem, so Track A would be false. Its native certificate is a PDS in a nonabelian semidirect-product group (Definition 3.1), and Theorem 4.8 plus Remark 4.9 construct it explicitly; the easy regime is exactly the displayed five-piece formula, with the \(q\equiv3\pmod4\) restriction and GAP nonexistence observations outside it. I’ll retain the transformation route, but enlarge the same-distribution decoy crowding at fixed witness size—the prior attempt only enlarged the modulus, which its transcript proves does not harden the task. The Track B comparison will be the measured per-row modular-recovery algorithm versus a cross-row invariant route, both stated honestly.
